        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Tomb-Raider-Legacy-of-Atlantis-(1).png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>Last year, on a bit of a whim, I ended up playing Tomb Raider 1's superb remaster <em>and</em> Crystal Dynamics' 2007 remake <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/tomb-raider-anniversary\">Tomb Raider: Anniversary</a>. Both, it turns out, are enormously enjoyable - and very different - ways to play Lara Croft's trailblazing original platform adventure, which celebrates its 30th anniversary this year. So I can understand why the minds behind Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis might want to do something beyond a slick visual overhaul. But after my latest Gamescom look, I'm not exactly convinced this remake - now due to arrive early next year - is heading the right way.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/tomb-raider-legacy-of-atlantis-gamescom-preview\">Read more</a></p>",
